" data-luma-option=\"C\"></span><span>visit the university</span></div></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":5},{"id":"en-trainer-1-t2-l-g3-1","type":"source_html","ieltsQuestionType":"matching_features","instructions":"","sourceHeading":"Questions 26-30","sourceHtml":"<div class=\"source-question-section-content\"><p>What does Chloe decide about the following subjects?</p><p>Write the correct letter, A, B or C, next to questions 26-30.</p></div><div class=\"source-questions\"><div class=\"matching-dnd-questions\"><div class=\"source-question-item\"> • Public relations<span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">26</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-trainer-1-t2-l-q26\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"> • Marketing<span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">27</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-trainer-1-t2-l-q27\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"> • Taxation<span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">28</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-trainer-1-t2-l-q28\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"> • Human resources<span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">29</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-trainer-1-t2-l-q29\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"> • Information systems<span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">30</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-trainer-1-t2-l-q30\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></div></div><div class=\"options-dnd-panel dnd-panel dnd-panel--matching\"><div class=\"dnd-panel-instruction\">Drag and drop an option to fill in each blank.</div><div class=\"dnd-cards-container\"><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"A\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">A.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">She will study it.</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"B\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">B.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">She won't study it.</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"C\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">C.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">She might study it.</span></div></div></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":5}],"audio_fallbacks":["https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/ielts_trainer_1_academic_listening_test_2_3.mp3"],"order_index":3},{"id":"en-trainer-1-t2-l-p4","title":"Part 4","part_number":4,"passage_text":"","audio_url":"https://ielts-listening-audio.engnovatemedia.com/3146565-ielts_trainer_1_academic_listening_test_2_4.mp3","question_groups":[{"id":"en-trainer-1-t2-l-g4-0","type":"source_html","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","instructions":"","sourceHeading":"Questions 31-35","sourceHtml":"<div class=\"source-question-section-content\"><div class=\"source-section-content-wrapper\"><p>Complete the notes below.</p><p>Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS for each answer.</p><div><strong>History of weather forecasting</strong></div><p><strong>Early methods</strong></p><ul><li>Almanacs connected the weather with the positions of different <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">31</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-trainer-1-t2-l-q31\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> at particular times.</li></ul><p><strong>Invention of weather instruments</strong></p><ul><li>A hygrometer showed levels of <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">32</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-trainer-1-t2-l-q32\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> (Nicholas Cusa 1450)</li><li>Temperature variations first measured by a thermometer containing <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">33</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-trainer-1-t2-l-q33\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> (Galileo Galilei 1593)</li><li>A barometer indicated air pressure (Evangelista Torricelli 1643)</li></ul><p><strong>Transmitting weather information</strong></p><ul><li>The use of the <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">34</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-trainer-1-t2-l-q34\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> allowed information to be passed around the world.</li><li>Daily <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">35</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-trainer-1-t2-l-q35\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> were produced by the French from 1863.</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"source-questions\"><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":5},{"id":"en-trainer-1-t2-l-g4-1","type":"source_html","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","instructions":"","sourceHeading":"Questions 36-40","sourceHtml":"<div class=\"source-question-section-content\"><div class=\"source-section-content-wrapper\"><p>Complete the sentences below.</p><p>Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS for each answer.</p><ul><li>Weather observation stations are found mostly at <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">36</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-trainer-1-t2-l-q36\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> around the country.</li><li>Satellite images use the colour orange to show <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">37</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-trainer-1-t2-l-q37\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> .</li><li>The satellites give so much detail that meteorologists can distinguish a particular <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">38</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-trainer-1-t2-l-q38\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> .</li><li>Information about the upper atmosphere is sent from instruments attached to a <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">39</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-trainer-1-t2-l-q39\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> .</li><li>Radar is particularly useful for following the movement of <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">40</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-trainer-1-t2-l-q40\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> .</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"source-questions\"><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":5}],"audio_fallbacks":["https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/ielts_trainer_1_academic_listening_test_2_4.mp3"],"order_index":4}],"questions":[{"id":"en-trainer-1-t2-l-q1","part_id":"en-trainer-1-t2-l-p1","group_id":"en-trainer-1-t2-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","question_text":"","correct_answer":"edwinari","correct_answer_variants":["edwinari"],"answerCount":1,"sourceNumbers":[1],"sourceInputName":"ielts_listening_answer_3146268_1","order_index":1,"points":1},{"id":"en-trainer-1-t2-l-q2","part_id":"en-trainer-1-t2-l-p1","group_id":"en-trainer-1-t2-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","question_text":"","correct_answer":"New Zealander","correct_answer_variants":["New Zealander"],"answerCount":1,"sourceNumbers":[2],"sourceInputName":"ielts_listening_answer_3146268_2","order_index":2,"points":1},{"id":"en-trainer-1-t2-l-q3","part_id":"en-trainer-1-t2-l-p1","group_id":"en-trainer-1-t2-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","question_text":"","correct_answer":"play centre/play center","correct_answer_variants":["pl